# docker volume notes

Why docker volumes?
==================

	Ø If the application is down wt will happen? --> app can't access, you may lose app data, files, folders, imp info etc.

Wt is docker volumes?
==================

	Ø Whenever your container will restart, crashed, goes down, not running still you can access your app data by docker volumes
	Ø Docker volumes will persist you app data even if your container got deleted.
	Ø Volumes is nothing but it’s a directory it means you are going to declare a directory as a volume.
	Ø Docker volumes will be created out of the file system it means volumes will not create inside the container.
	Ø It is better to create volumes along with the container becz after creation of container it is difficult to attach a volume to the container.
	Ø You can share one volume with no.of containers.

Docker volume types
=================

	Ø Docker has 3 type of volumes

	1. Anonymous volume --> it means there will be no meaningful name to the volume.
	2. Named volume --> it means you will be having a meaningful name to the volume.
	3. Bind Volume --> it means you are going to choose the location where you want to save your app data.

